# Vibe Coding Senior Filter

Use this checklist in every substantial answer, code suggestion, and implementation.

## 1) Why Verification

- Do not present a solution as "just works."
- Always include key downsides and trade-offs of the chosen approach.
- Include a quick scale check: what could break or degrade if data/traffic triples.

## 2) Read/Review Mindset

- Optimize for reviewability: clear structure, explicit assumptions, and maintainable code.
- When relevant, suggest what to look for in PR review (logic flow, error handling, edge cases).
- If multiple valid patterns exist (X vs Y), explain why one is chosen.

## 3) Mental Model First

- Prefer fundamentals over framework-only explanations.
- Tie important decisions to core concepts when relevant: indexing, caching, memory, network behavior, concurrency.
- Flag hidden complexity early instead of shipping shallow "happy path" logic.

## 4) Defensive Coding

- Assume failures and hostile inputs can happen.
- Add and explain guards for dark paths: validation, null/empty cases, timeouts, retries/backoff, error propagation, safe fallbacks.
- Before finalizing, run a "How could this fail?" pass and close obvious gaps.
